claims.what_is_true:
It caught 27 of 52. Gaps not listed anywhere:
- methods swapped between two real operations (ts list<->load, c update<->patch);
- parameter types and names (ts match?: object -> string, c voxgig_value* -> const char*, ts match -> id);
- clojure's declared returns, since its forms set returns and sigReturns to '' (list -> vector became -> map, not caught);
- a wrong type that is not 'any' where there is no canonToType column (zig INTEGER i64->f64, clojure long->string). perl and ocaml also have no column;
- a client member declared on the entity (utility() added to the entity, not caught, because entity signatures are searched in every file);
- the record printer disagreeing with the record fact.
Misses that are listed as unguarded: collection, noun, none, lits, nullValue, cancel, ctor, utility copy-or-live, direct returns, and c's ARRAY/OBJECT exception. Caught: method typos, optional->required, added and dropped parameters, py returns, style (ts, c, clojure), async, record, members removed or invented, and runtime renames and parameter changes (ts, clojure, c).

